/**
\fn pdg::ElementRef* pdg::Drawing::addText(const char* text, const Rect& rect, const Attributes& attrs)
\brief Add owned, editable UTF-8 text to drawing artwork.

Copies the text and attributes. Font, text size/style, fill color and fill opacity
follow Port::drawText(). Newlines are supported. The rectangle supplies the local
layout bounds and four corner control points; hit tests use its box. Element and
parent transforms and opacities apply normally, including live attributes.

Part/Sprite artwork snapshots preserve text and styling. Fonts are saved by name
and scaling factor, without embedding font files; the receiving system must supply
the font for the same appearance. Older drawing snapshots remain readable.

\param text Non-null, null-terminated UTF-8 text of at most 1 MiB; may be empty.
\param rect Finite local rectangle with right >= left and bottom >= top.
\param attrs Text appearance and transform to copy.
\return An owned ElementRef of type type_Text; the caller deletes this handle.

\note Rendering requires a graphics build. Attach the drawing with Part::setDrawing()
to include it in that owner's saved artwork.
\par Example
\code{.cpp}
std::unique_ptr<pdg::Drawing> drawing(pdg::Drawing::create());
pdg::Attributes attrs;
attrs.textSize(24).textStyle(pdg::textStyle_Bold).fillColor(pdg::Color(1.f, 1.f, 1.f));
std::unique_ptr<pdg::ElementRef> label(drawing->addText("Player 1", pdg::Rect(0, 0, 180, 40), attrs));
label->setText("Player 2");
\endcode
\see ElementRef::getText(), ElementRef::setText(), Part::setDrawing()
*/
/**
\fn const char* pdg::ElementRef::getText() const
\brief Get the text of a text element.
\return Borrowed null-terminated UTF-8 text, valid until the element's text changes
or its contents are removed. Throws for a non-text or removed element.
*/
/**
\fn void pdg::ElementRef::setText(const char* text)
\brief Copy new text into an element while retaining its rectangle and styling.
\param text Non-null, null-terminated UTF-8 text of at most 1 MiB; may be empty.
Throws for a non-text or removed element.
*/
